      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2016-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring the numerator gives \\[ \\begin{gathered} \\dfrac{11!-10!}{9!}\\\\ =\\dfrac{10!(11-1)}{9!}\\\\ =\\dfrac{10\\cdot 9!\\cdot 10}{9!}\\\\ =100. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(10!\\) out of the numerator",
        "\\(11!-10!=10!(11-1)\\) and \\(10!=10\\cdot 9!\\)"
      ],
